{
  "video_id": "16PhlyStJSU",
  "title": "The Claude Expert Speedrun Nobody's Doing",
  "description": "Most people use Claude at about 10% of what it can do. This is the 5-day setup that fixes it: build memory with Projects, teach it about you, turn on Cowork, connect your apps, then let Claude Code work on your computer. No coding required. The simple Claude tutorial for beginners. #Shorts #ClaudeAI #aitools \n\nGet the full 5-day roadmap here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N_VX9uL5yU5zFzzlElJjTuE2cNNu0JhRrOpboPbHcwo/edit?usp=sharing",
  "publishedAt": "2026-06-21T06:15:18Z",
  "channel_name": "Sebastian Hardy | AI Marketing",
  "transcript": "This is the official five-day guide that takes Claude beginners to expert. Most people download Claude, ask it a couple questions, and never touch the part that makes it actually useful. Here's the five-day setup that fixes that. Day one, you build its memory. You create four projects, one for your content, one for clients, one for operations, one for your personal stuff. So, it stops forgetting everything the second you close the chat. Day two, you teach it about you. You write two short files, one about your goals and background, one about how you want it to write and think, and you drop them into every project. Day three, it starts working on its own. You switch from the chat tab to co-work, and there's a guided setup built right in, so you just follow it. Day four is where it gets real power. Right now, it only knows what's inside the app, so you connect your apps, your drive, your Gmail, your calendar, and now it works across all of them. Day five, you unlock the full thing with Claude code. it access to your computer, and it does real jobs on its own. I told it to clear out my downloads folder, anything older than 30 days, and it was done in two minutes. Comment road map, and I'll send you the full five-day setup, every step laid out.",
